WEBVTT

00:00.550 --> 00:04.830
When we compare triangle
ABC to triangle XYZ,

00:04.830 --> 00:07.450
it's pretty clear that
they aren't congruent,

00:07.450 --> 00:11.300
that they have very different
lengths of their sides.

00:11.300 --> 00:13.130
But there does seem
to be something

00:13.130 --> 00:16.120
interesting about the
relationship between these two

00:16.120 --> 00:17.020
triangles.

00:17.020 --> 00:20.500
One, all of their corresponding
angles are the same.

00:20.500 --> 00:25.620
So the angle right here, angle
BAC, is congruent to angle YXZ.

00:25.620 --> 00:29.640
Angle BCA is congruent
to angle YZX,

00:29.640 --> 00:33.990
and angle ABC is
congruent to angle XYZ.

00:33.990 --> 00:37.550
So all of their corresponding
angles are the same.

00:37.550 --> 00:41.000
And we also see that
the sides are just

00:41.000 --> 00:43.600
scaled-up versions
of each other.

00:43.600 --> 00:50.380
So to go from the length of XZ
to AC, we can multiply by 3.

00:50.380 --> 00:52.320
We multiplied by 3 there.

00:52.320 --> 00:57.790
To go from the length of XY
to the length of AB, which

00:57.790 --> 01:01.960
is the corresponding side,
we are multiplying by 3.

01:01.960 --> 01:03.760
We have to multiply by 3.

01:03.760 --> 01:09.160
And then to go from the length
of YZ to the length of BC,

01:09.160 --> 01:13.702
we also multiplied by 3.

01:13.702 --> 01:16.830
So essentially,
triangle ABC is just

01:16.830 --> 01:19.830
a scaled-up version
of triangle XYZ.

01:19.830 --> 01:21.520
If they were the
same scale, they

01:21.520 --> 01:23.110
would be the exact
same triangles.

01:23.110 --> 01:25.162
But one is just a bigger,
a blown-up version

01:25.162 --> 01:25.870
of the other one.

01:25.870 --> 01:28.610
Or this is a miniaturized
version of that one over there.

01:28.610 --> 01:31.060
If you just multiply
all the sides by 3,

01:31.060 --> 01:32.700
you get to this triangle.

01:32.700 --> 01:34.230
And so we can't
call them congruent,

01:34.230 --> 01:37.320
but this does seem to be a
bit of a special relationship.

01:37.320 --> 01:40.720
So we call this special
relationship similarity.

01:40.720 --> 01:49.489
So we can write that triangle
ABC is similar to triangle--

01:49.489 --> 01:51.780
and we want to make sure we
get the corresponding sides

01:51.780 --> 01:55.126
right-- ABC is going
to be similar to XYZ.

01:59.810 --> 02:01.450
And so, based on
what we just saw,

02:01.450 --> 02:03.550
there's actually kind
of three ideas here.

02:03.550 --> 02:06.720
And they're all equivalent ways
of thinking about similarity.

02:06.720 --> 02:09.210
One way to think
about it is that one

02:09.210 --> 02:11.190
is a scaled-up
version of the other.

02:11.190 --> 02:17.850
So scaled-up or -down
version of the other.

02:17.850 --> 02:19.400
When we talked about
congruency, they

02:19.400 --> 02:20.680
had to be exactly the same.

02:20.680 --> 02:23.260
You could rotate it, you could
shift it, you could flip it.

02:23.260 --> 02:24.760
But when you do all
of those things,

02:24.760 --> 02:26.840
they would have to
essentially be identical.

02:26.840 --> 02:29.690
With similarity, you can
rotate it, you can shift it,

02:29.690 --> 02:30.460
you can flip it.

02:30.460 --> 02:33.980
And you can also scale it up
and down in order for something

02:33.980 --> 02:35.090
to be similar.

02:35.090 --> 02:44.310
So for example, let's
say triangle CDE,

02:44.310 --> 02:50.100
if we know that triangle CDE
is congruent to triangle FGH,

02:50.100 --> 02:52.450
then we definitely know
that they are similar.

02:52.450 --> 02:54.195
They are scaled up
by a factor of 1.

02:54.195 --> 02:57.680
Then we know, for a
fact, that CDE is also

02:57.680 --> 03:00.740
similar to triangle FGH.

03:00.740 --> 03:02.840
But we can't say it
the other way around.

03:02.840 --> 03:05.350
If triangle ABC
is similar to XYZ,

03:05.350 --> 03:07.430
we can't say that it's
necessarily congruent.

03:07.430 --> 03:09.140
And we see, for this
particular example,

03:09.140 --> 03:11.930
they definitely
are not congruent.

03:11.930 --> 03:13.965
So this is one way to
think about similarity.

03:13.965 --> 03:15.590
The other way to
think about similarity

03:15.590 --> 03:19.000
is that all of the corresponding
angles will be equal.

03:19.000 --> 03:22.520
So if something is similar, then
all of the corresponding angles

03:22.520 --> 03:23.890
are going to be congruent.

03:29.935 --> 03:31.990
I always have trouble
spelling this.

03:31.990 --> 03:41.835
It is 2 Rs, 1 S. Corresponding
angles are congruent.

03:44.370 --> 03:50.220
So if we say that triangle ABC
is similar to triangle XYZ,

03:50.220 --> 03:58.026
that is equivalent to saying
that angle ABC is congruent--

03:58.026 --> 03:59.650
or we could say that
their measures are

03:59.650 --> 04:01.136
equal-- to angle XYZ.

04:05.790 --> 04:13.405
That angle BAC is going to
be congruent to angle YXZ.

04:17.950 --> 04:24.880
And then finally,
angle ACB is going

04:24.880 --> 04:28.940
to be congruent to angle XZY.

04:35.080 --> 04:37.240
So if you have two triangles,
all of their angles

04:37.240 --> 04:39.490
are the same, then you could
say that they're similar.

04:39.490 --> 04:41.700
Or if you find two
triangles and you're

04:41.700 --> 04:43.474
told that they are
similar triangles,

04:43.474 --> 04:45.640
then you know that all of
their corresponding angles

04:45.640 --> 04:46.650
are the same.

04:46.650 --> 04:49.170
And the last way
to think about it

04:49.170 --> 04:52.120
is that the sides are all
just scaled-up versions

04:52.120 --> 04:53.180
of each other.

04:53.180 --> 04:58.450
So the sides scaled
by the same factor.

05:02.770 --> 05:05.191
In the example we did here,
the scaling factor was 3.

05:05.191 --> 05:06.190
It doesn't have to be 3.

05:06.190 --> 05:10.750
It just has to be the same
scaling factor for every side.

05:10.750 --> 05:13.560
If we scaled this side up by 3
and we only scaled this side up

05:13.560 --> 05:15.410
by 2, then we would
not be dealing

05:15.410 --> 05:17.110
with a similar triangle.

05:17.110 --> 05:19.230
But if we scaled all
of these sides up by 7,

05:19.230 --> 05:21.730
then that's still a similar,
as long as you have all of them

05:21.730 --> 05:25.240
scaled up or scaled down
by the exact same factor.

05:25.240 --> 05:28.964
So one way to think
about it is-- I

05:28.964 --> 05:30.630
want to still visualize
those triangles.

05:30.630 --> 05:33.010
Let me redraw them right over
here a little bit simpler.

05:33.010 --> 05:35.010
Because I'm not talking
in now in general terms,

05:35.010 --> 05:36.650
not even for that specific case.

05:36.650 --> 05:43.600
So if we say that this is A, B,
and C, and this right over here

05:43.600 --> 05:49.150
is X, Y, and Z. I
just redrew them

05:49.150 --> 05:52.110
so I can refer them
when we write down here.

05:52.110 --> 05:54.665
If we're saying that these
two things right over here

05:54.665 --> 05:57.680
are similar, that means
that corresponding sides

05:57.680 --> 05:59.530
are scaled-up versions
of each other.

05:59.530 --> 06:05.920
So we could say that
the length of AB

06:05.920 --> 06:08.110
is equal to some
scaling factor--

06:08.110 --> 06:10.640
and this thing could be
less than 1-- some scaling

06:10.640 --> 06:14.770
factor times the length of
XY, the corresponding sides.

06:14.770 --> 06:16.920
And I know that AB
corresponds to XY because

06:16.920 --> 06:20.180
of the order in which I wrote
this similarity statement.

06:20.180 --> 06:24.100
So some scaling factor times XY.

06:24.100 --> 06:30.000
We know that the
length of BC needs

06:30.000 --> 06:36.455
to be that same scaling
factor times the length of YZ.

06:44.270 --> 06:49.140
And then we know
the length of AC

06:49.140 --> 06:53.210
is going to be equal to that
same scaling factor times XZ.

06:53.210 --> 06:56.840
So that's XZ, and this
could be a scaling factor.

06:56.840 --> 07:01.470
So if ABC is larger
than XYZ, then

07:01.470 --> 07:03.390
these k's will be larger than 1.

07:03.390 --> 07:05.640
If they're the exact same
size, if they're essentially

07:05.640 --> 07:08.630
congruent triangles,
then these k's will be 1.

07:08.630 --> 07:12.420
And if XYZ is bigger
than ABC, then

07:12.420 --> 07:15.361
these [? scaling ?] factors
will be less than 1.

07:15.361 --> 07:17.860
But another way to write these
same statements-- notice, all

07:17.860 --> 07:19.235
I'm saying is
corresponding sides

07:19.235 --> 07:21.150
are scaled-up versions
of each other.

07:21.150 --> 07:24.710
This first statement right here,
if you divide both sides by XY,

07:24.710 --> 07:31.720
you get AB over XY is equal
to our scaling factor.

07:31.720 --> 07:33.470
And then the second
statement right

07:33.470 --> 07:37.320
over here, if you divide
both sides by YZ--

07:37.320 --> 07:39.400
let me do it in that
same color-- you

07:39.400 --> 07:47.557
get BC divided by YZ is
equal to that scaling factor.

07:47.557 --> 07:49.390
And remember, in the
example we just showed,

07:49.390 --> 07:52.512
that scaling factor was 3.

07:52.512 --> 07:54.970
But now we're saying in the
more general terms, similarity,

07:54.970 --> 07:57.370
as long as you have the
same scaling factor.

07:57.370 --> 07:59.280
And then finally, if
you divide both sides

07:59.280 --> 08:04.210
here by the length between X
and Z, or segment XZ's length,

08:04.210 --> 08:11.390
you get AC over XZ is
equal to k, as well.

08:11.390 --> 08:13.620
Or another way to think
about it is the ratio

08:13.620 --> 08:14.980
between corresponding sides.

08:14.980 --> 08:18.990
Notice, this is the
ratio between AB and XY.

08:18.990 --> 08:27.460
The ratio between BC and YZ,
the ratio between AC and XZ,

08:27.460 --> 08:29.590
that the ratio between
corresponding sides

08:29.590 --> 08:31.990
all gives us the same constant.

08:31.990 --> 08:37.059
Or you could rewrite
this as AB over XY

08:37.059 --> 08:48.050
is equal to BC over YZ is equal
to AC over XZ, which would be

08:48.050 --> 08:51.214
equal to some scaling
factor, which is equal to k.

08:51.214 --> 08:52.630
So if you have
similar triangles--

08:52.630 --> 08:54.580
let me draw an arrow
right over here.

08:54.580 --> 08:56.962
Similar triangles means that
they're scaled-up versions,

08:56.962 --> 08:59.170
and you can also flip and
rotate and do all the stuff

08:59.170 --> 09:00.450
with congruency.

09:00.450 --> 09:02.500
And you can scale
them up or down.

09:02.500 --> 09:04.390
Which means all of the
corresponding angles

09:04.390 --> 09:06.940
are congruent, which
also means that the ratio

09:06.940 --> 09:08.970
between corresponding
sides is going

09:08.970 --> 09:11.580
to be the same constant for
all the corresponding sides.

09:11.580 --> 09:14.360
Or the ratio between
corresponding sides

09:14.360 --> 09:15.942
is constant.
